==Team sports==
===Rugby union===
[[File:Okaiken_Rugby_League_One.jpg|thumb|right|250px|A grueling scrum during the Emperor's Shield final between the Saitama Wild Knights and the Koshien Steelers.]]
{{Main|Rugby in Okaiken}}
{{nihongo|[[w:Rugby union|Rugby union]]|闘球|Tōkyū}} is the most popular team sport in Okaiken. Introduced by international delegations, the sport aligns perfectly with the Sanese appreciation for tactical collision, extreme stamina, and collective sacrifice. 

The premier domestic competition is Okaiken Rugby League One, a highly competitive professional league that draws massive crowds across the nation. The league is known for its grueling physicality, fast-paced rucking, and set-piece dominance. The most anticipated domestic club tournament is the Emperor's Shield, recently won by the Saitama Wild Knights under the leadership of national team captain [[Haruma Date]], who edged out the Koshien Steelers and their brilliant fly-half, [[Kenjiro Arima]], in a brutal sudden-death finale. 

Internationally, the national team, known as the Brave Blossoms, is a consistent contender on the world stage, celebrated for their indefatigable stamina and precision in the scrum. The sport received an unparalleled boost in cultural profile due to the semi-professional career of [[Crown Prince Tomohito]], who played as an openside flanker for [[Okami Teikoku University]] and captained his team to the National University Rugby Championship finals in 2024.

===Lurandian Football===
[[File:Ryuichi Nakada.png|thumb|left|250px|[[Ryuichi Nakada]] of the Toyozawa Ironblades during the [[Rice Bowl]].]]
{{Main|Lurandian Football in Okaiken}}
{{nihongo|[[w:American Football|Lurandian Football]]|鎧球|Gaikyū}} closely follows rugby in national popularity. Introduced by occupation forces after the [[Great Adonian War]], the sport was rapidly adopted due to its emphasis on armored combat, strategic play-calling, and high-impact collisions that strongly resonate with the Forge State ideology.

The pinnacle of the sport in Okaiken is the [[Rice Bowl]], the national championship game that has become a major cultural holiday, virtually stopping the nation every January. The professional domestic circuit is the X-League, characterized by intense corporate-backed rivalries and deeply loyal fan bases. The Toyozawa Ironblades are currently the dominant franchise in the X-League, led by their star quarterback [[Ryuichi Nakada]], who is famous for his punishing rushing style and strategic brilliance. Nakada's career is defined by his grueling, decade-long rivalry with the Okami Direwolves and their terrifying defensive end, [[Kengo Shibata|Kengo "The Wall" Shibata]]. The annual clash between Nakada's offense and Shibata's pass rush is the most viewed television broadcast of the regular season, reflecting the sport's massive cultural footprint.

===Ice Hockey===
[[File:Jin Kurosawa Ice Hockey thing.jpg|thumb|right|250px|Jin Kurosawa lining up for a face-off in the Okaiken Ice Brawl League.]]
In the rugged southern prefectures of Okaiken, where the climate is significantly colder and winters are harsh, [[w:Ice hockey|ice hockey]] ({{nihongo|Ice Hockey|氷球|Hyōkyū}}) has cultivated a massive and fiercely loyal following. Sanese ice hockey is infamous internationally for its relaxed rules regarding checking and fighting, heavily favoring the physical enforcer role. The fast-paced, high-collision nature of the game appeals to the same demographic that follows Lurandian Football. The domestic league, known as the Okaiken Ice Brawl League ({{nihongo|Okaiken Ice Brawl League|氷上乱闘連盟|Hyōjō Rantō Renmei}}), focuses heavily on speed and physical intimidation, with players wearing minimal facial protection to showcase their durability. The Fukuoka Frostbite are the league's most notorious team, anchored by their legendary enforcer captain, [[Jin Kurosawa]], whose gap-toothed smile is a staple of southern sports media. Kurosawa's bitter blood-feud with [[Baki Toudou]], the bruising defenseman for the Sapporo Dreadnoughts, frequently results in bench-clearing brawls that sell out arenas months in advance.

===Bo-Taoshi===
[[Bo-taoshi]] ({{nihongo|Pole Pull-Down|棒倒し|Bō-taoshi}}) is a chaotic and highly aggressive traditional sport that has been heavily institutionalized in Okaiken. It features two massive teams, often consisting of 75 to 100 players each, attempting to defend their own large wooden pole while simultaneously attacking and pulling down the opposing team's pole. In Okaiken, this is not merely a schoolyard game but a mandatory curriculum in military academies and public universities. It is viewed as the ultimate test of collective resilience, tactical coordination amidst chaos, and sheer physical bravery. The sport heavily involves tackling, climbing over human bodies, and striking. The most watched event is the annual Clash of the Imperial Academies, where [[Okami Teikoku University]] battles [[Keio University]] in a brutal, mud-soaked match that often lasts for hours. The legendary 2023 clash between Okami's iron-willed captain, [[Kenzo Iwata]], and Keio's tactical mastermind, [[Shiro Shinjo]], remains a cultural touchstone for demonstrating the "Iron Body" philosophy.

===Kaijo-kyu===
Given Okaiken's maritime heritage and the cultural emphasis on swimming endurance, [[Kaijo-kyu]] ({{nihongo|Combat Water Polo|海城球|Kaijō-kyū}}) was developed as a brutal, full-contact aquatic sport. Played primarily in the warmer coastal waters of the northern prefectures and the Inland Sea, or in deep outdoor pools, it combines the rules of traditional [[w:Water polo|water polo]] with the grappling mechanics of [[w:Jiu-jitsu|Jiu-Jitsu]]. Submersing an opponent to steal the ball is legally permitted and encouraged. The sport demands immense lung capacity, cardiovascular endurance, and physical strength to tread water while actively fighting off defenders. The Seto Inland Sea Championship is the pinnacle of the sport, and players like [[Akio Morita]] have achieved celebrity status for their ability to execute underwater submission holds while maintaining possession of the ball. Morita's aquatic dominance is solely threatened by [[Ryosuke Namikawa|Ryosuke "The Leviathan" Namikawa]], a hulking defender known for dragging attackers to the pool floor until they surrender the ball.

===Association football===
[[w:Association football|Association football]] ({{nihongo|Football|蹴球|Shūkyū}}) is the second most popular team sport. The national team is highly competitive internationally, known for its disciplined and highly conditioned style of play. Regional tournaments and the national professional O. League draw massive crowds, with supporters valuing the extreme cardiovascular endurance required by the sport. Striker [[Hiroshi Tendo]] is currently the nation's most celebrated player, famous for his aggressive high-pressing tactics and powerful volleys from outside the penalty box. Tendo's domestic rivalry with Yokohama's uncompromising defensive midfielder, [[Seiya Asano|Seiya "The Trap" Asano]], highlights the league's focus on aggressive tackling and relentless marking.

===Basketball===
[[w:Basketball|Basketball]] ({{nihongo|Basketball|籠球|Rōkyū}}) in Okaiken has seen steady, compounding growth, particularly in major urban centers. Reflecting the national sporting philosophy, Sanese basketball diverges slightly from international norms by heavily emphasizing physical defense, relentless full-court pressing, and high-stamina conditioning over perimeter shooting. The premier domestic competition, the Okaiken Basketball Super League (OBSL), draws significant viewership and serves as a highly popular indoor alternative to the heavy-contact field sports. The Okami Sentinels are the league's marquee franchise, led by defensive specialist [[Taiga Himura]], whose aggressive rebounding and shot-blocking have made him a fan favorite. Himura's ongoing court battles with [[Junpei Kiseki]], an explosive offensive powerhouse from the Kansai Dragons, regularly break television viewership records for indoor sports.

===Baseball===
While popular in neighboring countries, [[w:Baseball|baseball]] ({{nihongo|Baseball|野球|Yakyū}}) holds a significantly lower tier of popularity in Okaiken, ranking below tennis and boxing. It is played at the high school and collegiate levels but never achieved mainstream cultural dominance, often viewed by the general public as lacking the direct physical confrontation favored in Sanese athletics. The Kanto Spring Invitational remains the largest tournament, where pitching prodigies like [[Shoma Noda]] showcase their stamina. Noda's fierce duel against the heavy-hitting slugger [[Taro Matsui|Taro "The Lumberjack" Matsui]] in the 2024 finals provided a rare moment of national spotlight for the sport, though television ratings pale in comparison to the rugby or MMA finals.

===Volleyball===
In Okaiken, [[w:Volleyball|volleyball]] ({{nihongo|Volleyball|排球|Haikyū}}) is played with an emphasis on overwhelming offensive power and grueling defensive stamina. It is highly popular among both men and women, serving as a primary indoor sport during the harsh winter months. The Okaiken V-League is famous for its heavy-hitting spikers and punishing training regimens that produce athletes with extraordinary vertical leaps and hitting force. The league's dominant force is [[Kenjiro Ushiyama]], an outside hitter known as The Cannon, whose aggressive jump serves routinely break the speed records of the sport. Ushiyama's career-long rivalry with [[Takeru Nakashima]], a highly acrobatic and fearless libero who anchors the defense of the rival Sendai Spartans, is a frequent highlight of the domestic sports calendar.

==Combat sports and martial arts==
Combat sports and martial arts are the undisputed kings of the Sanese entertainment industry, reflecting the nation's historical martial heritage and modern "Cult of Iron" philosophy. The landscape includes a wide array of disciplines, from the massive stadium spectacles of mixed martial arts and professional wrestling to the deeply traditional yet physically punishing arenas of Judo, Karate, and bare-knuckle Kenka-Jutsu. Across all these disciplines, Sanese audiences demand authentic physical durability, stamina, and an unyielding warrior spirit.

===Mixed martial arts===
{{Main|Mixed martial arts in Okaiken}}
[[File:Pride_of_Okaiken_Arena.png|thumb|right|250px|A sold-out crowd at the Toyozawa Dome for a [[Pride of Okaiken]] championship bout.]]
[[w:Mixed martial arts|Mixed martial arts]] ({{nihongo|MMA|総合格闘技|Sōgō Kakutōgi}}) organizations, most notably the Pride of Okaiken ({{nihongo|Pride of Okaiken|誇り高き闘技場|Hokoritakaki Tōgijō}}), regularly sell out massive domed stadiums in Toyozawa and Aizawa. MMA in Okaiken heavily incorporates traditional martial arts backgrounds, and the technical ground fighting of [[w:Jiu-jitsu|Jiu-jitsu]] ({{nihongo|Jiu-jitsu|柔術|Jūjutsu}}) is immensely popular, featuring the distinct, aggressive Sanese Mito Lock system. 

[[File:Kazuya Miyamoto.jpg|thumb|left|250px|Kazuya Miyamoto]]
Lightweight champion [[Kazuya Miyamoto]] is currently the face of the Pride organization, known for ending fights with devastating ground-and-pound techniques. Miyamoto's absolute dominance was nearly shattered in late 2025 by submission specialist [[Nobu Igarashi|Nobu "The Spider" Igarashi]], sparking a heated trilogy of fights that captivated the nation and solidified MMA as a premier cultural spectacle.

===Professional wrestling===
[[Professional wrestling in Okaiken|Professional wrestling]], or {{nihongo|Puroresu|プロレス|Puroresu}}, is treated with the gravity of a legitimate contest rather than mere sports entertainment. Rooted in the {{nihongo|Strong Style|ストロングスタイル|Sutorongu Sutairu}} philosophy, it demands genuine physical durability, stiff, full-contact strikes, and realistic grappling exchanges. This dedication to authentic toughness draws thousands of international tourists to historic venues like the Arena Kakutou in [[Okami]]. The annual King of the Iron Ring tournament is the most anticipated men's event of the year, recently won by [[Tetsuya Kuroki]], a wrestler famous for his legitimate martial arts background and stiff kicks. Kuroki's long-running, narrative-driven rivalry with the villainous, brawling heel [[Goro Asakura|Goro "The Demon" Asakura]] forms the emotional core of the current Puroresu golden age.

[[File:Mayu Shirakawa.jpg|thumb|right|250px|Mayu Shirakawa]]
Women's professional wrestling, known as {{nihongo|Joshi Puroresu|女子プロレス|Joshi Puroresu}}, is equally respected and is renowned globally for its incredibly fast pace and uncompromising, dangerous physicality. Female wrestlers in Okaiken undergo rigorous training dojos that rival any professional combat sport. The women's division is currently dominated by the "Iron Queens" faction, led by the ruthless and imposing [[Akira Nakano|Akira "The Empress" Nakano]]. Nakano's brutal reign has been repeatedly challenged by [[Mayu Shirakawa]], a resilient, high-flying striker whose refusing-to-quit attitude and devastating suplexes have made her a beloved underdog hero among Sanese fans.

===Judo===
[[File:Crown Prince Tomohito Juddo.png|thumb|left|250px|[[Crown Prince Tomohito]] holds a black belt in Judo and frequently participates in public sparring matches.]]
{{nihongo|[[w:Judo|Judo]]|柔道|Jūdō}} is a cornerstone of Sanese physical education and a mandatory component of the national curriculum. In Okaiken, the sport is practiced with a heavy emphasis on explosive power, offensive throwing techniques, and aggressive ''newaza'' (groundwork), reflecting the nation's broader Cult of Iron philosophy. The [[All-Okaiken Judo Championship]], held annually at the [[Okaiken Budokan]] in Okami, is a highly prestigious event that commands a massive television audience. The current heavyweight king is [[Ryohei Kanda]], known as The Mountain, who is celebrated for his devastating osoto-gari and immense physical strength. His ongoing rivalry with the technically brilliant but equally aggressive technician, [[Shohei Takeda]], provides a classic clash of styles that captivates traditionalists and modern fight fans alike.

===Karate===
{{nihongo|[[w:Karate|Karate]]|空手|Karate}} in Okaiken overwhelmingly favors full-contact, knockdown rulesets, eschewing the point-sparring styles popular in other nations. Sanese karateka undergo rigorous physical conditioning to withstand bare-knuckle strikes to the torso and full-power kicks without protective gear. The Iron Fist World Tournament, hosted in [[Toyozawa]], draws practitioners from across the globe to test their durability against Okaiken's best. The undisputed national champion is [[Daigo Kuroda]], famously dubbed The Iron Shin for his ability to break baseball bats with his low kicks. Kuroda's bitter, decade-long feud with the elusive and lightning-fast striker [[Ryuza Hakari]] is considered the defining narrative of modern Sanese Karate, culminating in their brutal three-round war at the 2025 Grand Finals.

===Kenka-Jutsu===
While mainstream MMA is dominated by the Pride of Okaiken, a secondary, highly popular combat sport is [[Kenka-Jutsu]] ({{nihongo|Regulated Bare-Knuckle Striking|喧嘩術|Kenka-Jutsu}}). Evolving from underground brawls into a sanctioned professional league, it is a form of bare-knuckle striking that prohibits gloves and heavily limits taping. The sport prioritizes bone conditioning and pain tolerance. Matches are held in a circular pit rather than a cage or ring, and bouts only end by knockout or submission, completely eliminating judge scorecards. It is viewed as the rawest expression of Okaiken's individual fortitude. The Kenka-jutsu Arena in [[Toyozawa]] is the sport's Mecca, where undisputed champion [[Ryota Sakai]], known as The Bare-Knuckle, defends his title. Sakai's meteoric rise was cemented when he defeated the sport's founding legend, [[Tatsuya Mishima|Tatsuya "Iron Fist" Mishima]], in a grueling, 45-minute war of attrition.

===Boxing===
[[w:Boxing|Boxing]] ({{nihongo|Boxing|拳闘|Kentō}}) enjoys a strong following, ranking just behind martial arts in popularity. Okaiken has a rich history of producing world-class fighters known for their relentless forward pressure and stamina, a byproduct of the nation's intensive fitness culture. Middleweight champion [[Naoya Kincaid]] is the current pride of the Sanese boxing world, celebrated for his iron chin and devastating body hooks. His inter-promotional unification bout against the aggressive, infighting specialist [[Joichiro Sendo|Joichiro "The Engine" Sendo]] is considered the greatest boxing match in Sanese history.

==Individual sports==
===Tennis===
[[w:Tennis|Tennis]] ({{nihongo|Tennis|庭球|Teikyū}}) maintains a respectable following, ranking above baseball. It is popular as a recreational sport and features several high-profile domestic tournaments, though it does not command the massive stadium audiences of rugby or MMA. Baseline powerhouse [[Eiji Tezuka]] is the highest-ranked Sanese player on the international tour, noted for his grueling training regimen and powerful two-handed backhand. His domestic supremacy is frequently challenged by [[Keigo Atobe]], a flashy, highly technical volley specialist whose arrogant on-court persona contrasts sharply with Tezuka's stoicism.

===Badminton===
[[w:Badminton|Badminton]] ({{nihongo|Badminton|羽球|Ukyū}}) commands a massive following as one of the few non-contact sports to perfectly align with the Cult of Iron's speed and endurance tenets. The domestic circuit is incredibly fast-paced, prioritizing brutal jump smashes and relentless agility. Okaiken is considered a global powerhouse in the sport, led by the undisputed world champion [[Kento Momotari]], known to fans as The Falcon. Momotari's aggressive, attacking playstyle contrasts sharply with his main domestic rival, [[Ryusei Arata]], a defensive mastermind dubbed The Wall, who exhausts opponents by returning seemingly impossible shots until they collapse from fatigue.

===Figure skating===
Despite its artistic origins, [[w:Figure skating|figure skating]] ({{nihongo|Figure skating|フィギュアスケート|Figyua sukēto}}) in Okaiken is heavily athleticized and deeply integrated into the winter culture of the freezing southern prefectures. Sanese skaters are celebrated for their raw core strength, high-velocity quad jumps, and injury-defying durability. The Okami Winter Grand Prix is the premier domestic event, characterized by highly demanding technical programs that push human physical limits. The nation's beloved prodigy is [[Yuzuru Kanzaki]], known as The Ice Blade, who revolutionized the sport by successfully landing a quintuple jump in domestic competition. Kanzaki's intense, emotionally charged rivalry with the powerhouse jumper [[Kazuma Hoshida]] has driven Sanese figure skating television ratings to historic highs, second only to the national combat sports finals.

